    "done_when": "imas_ink/extract.py defines extract_signal_traces(ids, path) and imas_ink exports it. It returns one TimeSeries per filled element of every struct array the unindexed data-dictionary path passes through: values from the node's data; time from ids.time when ids_properties.homogeneous_time is 1 and from the node's own time when it is 0; ValueError for 2; unit from node.data.metadata.units; ylabel from the element's non-empty name, else the path's leading component; no label. Empty data is skipped, and a path containing '[' raises ValueError naming the unindexed form. No scaling, filtering or resampling.\ntests/unit/ink/test_signal_traces.py builds IDS in memory with imas.IDSFactory and asserts six things: a pf_active with three coils, one unfed, yields two series named by coil with unit A and time ids.time; a magnetics ip yields one series 'ip' in A; a magnetics under homogeneous time 0 takes each flux loop's own flux.time with unit Wb; homogeneous time 2 raises; the coil current path written with an index in square brackets after coil raises; no series has a label.\nGates: 'uv run --no-sync pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q tests/unit' adds no failure and 'uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ink tests' adds no finding, both against the base revision. Run them in place: this host is already a compute node (SLURM_JOB_ID set).",
